From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:00:50 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 40/57] PROTOTYPE pvr: PVR_TWIDDLE_ALL=1 turns the linear
 window-size rule off

Local switch for the shared amazon-suez/amazon-sheldonp stack. Both
devices' linear-layout patches had an off switch only on amazon-sheldonp
(PVR_TWIDDLE_ALL); keep it, so a layout A/B needs no rebuild (used on
2026-11-19 to show linear R8 samples right on a GE8300).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_image.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_image.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_image.c
index 5ef5cc12ac1..dca27918eeb 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_image.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_image.c
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
 #include "pvr_tex_state.h"
 #include "hwdef/rogue_hw_utils.h"
 #include "util/macros.h"
+#include "util/u_debug.h"
 #include "util/u_math.h"
 #include "vk_format.h"
 #include "vk_image.h"
@@ -58,6 +59,10 @@ static bool pvr_image_twiddle_padding_is_wasteful(const struct pvr_image *image)
    const uint64_t w = image->vk.extent.width;
    const uint64_t h = image->vk.extent.height;
 
+   /* PVR_TWIDDLE_ALL=1 keeps every optimal image twiddled, to compare. */
+   if (debug_get_bool_option("PVR_TWIDDLE_ALL", false))
+      return false;
+
    if (image->vk.image_type != VK_IMAGE_TYPE_2D || image->vk.mip_levels > 1 ||
        image->vk.array_layers > 1 || image->vk.samples > VK_SAMPLE_COUNT_1_BIT)
       return false;
